1. sudo modprobe i2c-dev
2. To make this permanent, add it to /etc/modules-load.d/i2c.conf:
    i2c-dev
3. sudo pacman -S ddcutil
4. ddcutil detect
5. check current brightness
    ddcutil getvcp 10
6. set brightness:
    ddcutil setvcp 10 50

Method 2: brightnessctl (Unified Control for Internal & External)

If you want a lightweight tool that can control both your laptop screen and external monitors seamlessly using backlight/DDC/CI protocols:

    Install brightnessctl:
    Bash

    sudo pacman -S brightnessctl

    List available devices:
    Bash

    brightnessctl --list

    Control brightness:
    Bash

    brightnessctl --device="ddc:0" set 50%
